All of netopen.c's `#include`s sit inside the `#if defined (HAVE_NETWORK)`
block, but the `#else` branch still calls `internal_error()` and `_()`.  With a
compiler that treats implicit function declarations as an error -- which GCC 14
and any C23 mode do -- that branch fails to compile:

    netopen.c:332:3: error: implicit declaration of function 'internal_error'
    netopen.c:332:19: error: implicit declaration of function '_'

Platforms with a full sockets API never take this branch, which is why it has
rotted unnoticed.  illumos does take it: `getpeername` lives in `libsocket`
rather than `libc`, so bash's `AC_CHECK_FUNCS([getpeername])` fails and
`config-bot.h` leaves `HAVE_NETWORK` undefined.

Pull in the three headers the stub actually needs.

--- lib/sh/netopen.c
+++ lib/sh/netopen.c
@@ -326,6 +326,11 @@
 
 #else /* !HAVE_NETWORK */
 
+#include <stdio.h>
+#include <bashansi.h>
+#include <bashintl.h>
+#include <shell.h>
+
 int
 netopen (char *path)
 {
